# BENEFITS REALISTION AND PERFORMANCE MANAGEMENT 

## Purpose

The purpose of this Benefits Realisation Plan is to define how the Emergency Department Patient Flow Transformation project will measure, track, and sustain improvements after implementation.

The objective of the project is not only to deliver a digital solution but to achieve measurable improvements in patient flow, operational efficiency, staff experience, and quality of care.



# Benefits Realisation Approach

Benefits will be managed throughout the project lifecycle by:

- Identifying expected benefits
- Defining measurable success indicators
- Establishing baseline performance
- Tracking improvements after implementation
- Taking corrective actions where benefits are not achieved



# Expected Project Benefits

The project is expected to deliver benefits across four key areas:

1. Patient Experience
2. Operational Efficiency
3. Staff Experience
4. Organisational Performance



# Patient Experience Benefits

## Benefit 1: Reduced Emergency Department Waiting Times

Current Challenge:

Patients experience delays before assessment, treatment, and transfer.

Expected Improvement:

Improved patient movement through better visibility of bed availability and faster decision-making.

Measurement:

- Average waiting time
- Time from arrival to treatment
- Time from decision to admit to ward transfer

Target Improvement:

Reduce average waiting times by 20%.



## Benefit 2: Improved Patient Experience

Current Challenge:

Long waits can negatively affect patient satisfaction.

Expected Improvement:

Patients receive faster and more coordinated care.

Measurement:

- Patient satisfaction surveys
- Complaints related to delays
- Feedback scores

Target Improvement:

Increase patient satisfaction scores by 15%.



# Operational Efficiency Benefits

## Benefit 3: Improved Bed Management

Current Challenge:

Bed availability information is often delayed or manually managed.

Expected Improvement:

Real-time visibility of hospital capacity.

Measurement:

- Bed allocation time
- Number of delayed transfers
- Bed utilisation rates

Target Improvement:

Reduce bed allocation delays by 30%.



## Benefit 4: Reduced Manual Administrative Work

Current Challenge:

Staff spend significant time manually collecting and communicating information.

Expected Improvement:

Automation and improved visibility reduce administrative workload.

Measurement:

- Time spent on manual reporting
- Number of manual processes replaced

Target Improvement:

Reduce manual administrative activities by 25%.



# Staff Experience Benefits

## Benefit 5: Improved Decision-Making Support

Current Challenge:

Healthcare teams often make decisions using incomplete information.

Expected Improvement:

Access to accurate real-time information.

Measurement:

- Staff feedback
- Decision-making confidence
- System usage statistics

Target Improvement:

Increase staff confidence in patient flow decisions.



# Organisational Benefits

## Benefit 6: Better Resource Utilisation

Current Challenge:

Hospital resources are not always used efficiently.

Expected Improvement:

Improved allocation of beds and staff resources.

Measurement:

- Bed occupancy levels
- Patient flow performance
- Operational efficiency indicators

Target Improvement:

Improve hospital capacity management.



# Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

Project performance will be monitored using measurable indicators.



## Patient Flow KPIs

KPIs include:

- Emergency Department waiting time
- Time to clinical assessment
- Admission processing time
- Transfer delays



## Technology KPIs

KPIs include:

- System availability
- User adoption rate
- Number of system issues
- Response time



## Adoption KPIs

KPIs include:

- Staff training completion
- Active system users
- User satisfaction scores
- Feedback results



## Financial KPIs

KPIs include:

- Budget performance
- Cost savings achieved
- Operational efficiency improvements



